docs/METAL_PROGRESS.md:295:**KV fp16 exception cells in production — machinery ships default-off; the attrib tail selection did NOT transfer, production re-selection says the event is ALL of layer 7 (2026-07-17 02:30–04:00, 16 GB mini; plan+gates: 2026-07-17-kv-except-production.md, logs/kv_except/).** operator-approved design step. Implementation (zero production-kernel changes, no ABI bump): per masked head, a kv_heads=1 fp16 side cache in the turbo3 WHT domain, an additive head-rows side-store kernel + causal window kernel (explicit out_row_stride), and window re-dispatches of the existing f16 attention over the masked head's 6-query window that overwrite the production output rows before the shared inverse WHT; `Q27_METAL_KV_FP16_CELLS` env (census cells, K+V pairs enforced), bytes in the engine reservation, snapshots refuse (v1), fp16 engines ignore the env. Gates: default-off byte-identical + suite green; new unit test (side store bit-exact, both windows overwrite exactly, zero leakage); ALL-cells probe collapses KL to the envelope floor (2.2e-4 mean — machinery correct end-to-end). **The scientific result: gate 3 with the instrument-selected cells 10,11 FAILED its kill line (max 2.265 @1000 vs band ≤1.30; mean in band) — instrument→production transfer holds for means, fails at the knife-edge tail.** Production re-selection (17 layer arms + L7 decomposition, 1,536-position arms ~2 min each): only FULL layer 7 kills the event (2.77→0.67; singles 2.2–2.7; **h0+h1 amplifies vs its own singles, 2.35** — the 4b anti-additive class again); L3 nearly (0.879), L19/L35 halve, 12 layers inert. **Formal 8K gate with L7-full (8 cells, +25.8% KV bytes): PASS — max 2.94→0.755 (3.9×, pos-1000 gone), mean −11%, wall +0.7%.** Disposition handed to operator: fund L7-full at +25.8%, design a mid-rate code (~+12.9%, unmeasured, amplification risk), or the uniform null. Attrib instrument demoted to means-only; production 1,536-pos arms are the tail standard now. **DECIDED (2026-07-17, operator: "fund full l7"): option 1 funded — `Q27_METAL_KV_FP16_CELLS=8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15` is the blessed turbo3 long-context production setting** (landing smoke: engine ctor accepts the list; server boots under it with the loud prefix-cache-DISABLED note and serves greedy). Funded residue: v1's snapshot refusal / prefix-cache disable is now a live production cost — side-cache snapshot serialization (v2) is the registered follow-up.
